   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI_16">192 rue de Grenelle</name>
                            </addrLine>                                	<addrLine>Paris</addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <salute>Dear budgen</salute>
                    </opener>
                    <p>        	I am very glad to hear that you are well and that <name type="person" key="schw99">Schwarz</name> thinks he has a buyer for the fine <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">portrait</seg> you did of me in Zurich. I would have added it to my small gallery but I have already about 30 canvasses on a limited wallspace to which <name type="person" key="john78">Augustus John</name> has just adde<supplied reason="off-margin">d</supplied> the fine drawing he made last week. I like the pose in your portrait but for the love of <name type="person" key="manf19">Manfield</name> tell the buyer that my size in shoes is a small seven.</p>
                    <p>        	I hope you will have better luck with your house after Xmas. Money is tied at this time. I am kep<supplied reason="off-margin">t</supplied> here for some days still.</p>
                    <p>        	I typed this myself.</p>
                    <p>Kind greetings to <name type="person" key="budg96">Mrs Budgen</name> and yourself and remember us to the <name type="person" key="sarg81">sargent</name>
                        <lb/>
                        <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                    </p>
                    <dateline>
                        <date when="1930-11-16">16 Nov 193o</date>
                    </dateline>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="global-note1" type="global">Since this was typed by Joyce, spacing has been normalized but spelling follows the original letter.</note>
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">The portrait is the oil painting of Joyce in a semi-reclining and somewhat convoluted pose (now held at the <rs type="external" key="http://onlinecollection.nationalgallery.ie/objects/8689/portrait-of-james-joyce-18821941-author?ctx=c9f56230-405a-4f2b-9a51-6f6efc7da5c4&amp;idx=0">National Gallery of Ireland</rs>) that Budgen used as the frontispiece for the first edition of <name type="work">JJMU</name>. The painting prominently displays Joyce’s right shoe. Thanks to Aaron M. Lisec of Southern Illinois University for identifying the location of the painting.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
